<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/305624956%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Trevinano";
    rdfs:comment "Trevinano is a human settlement in Italy, located in the Province of Viterbo of northern Lazio. In antiquity the site was settled by Etruscans. In the eleventh century, the powerful Boncompagni-Ludovisi family built a castle there.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/305624956> .

