<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/305879597%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Rabati Malik";
    rdfs:comment "An eleventh-century caravanserai along the Silk Road, now located in Uzbekistan. Rabati Malik Caravanserai was built under Karakhanid Shams-al-Mulk Nasr, son of Tamgachkhan Ibragim who ruled in Samarkand from 1068 to 1080. The site was added to the UNESCO World Heritage Tentative List in 2008.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/305879597> .

