<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/310920749%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Spetisbury Rings";
    rdfs:comment "Spetisbury Rings, also known as Crawford Castle, is a hillfort with Pre-Roman Iron Age earthen embankment fortifications located in north Dorset, England, near the River Stour. Tradition holds that invading Romans razed this indigenous stronghold in the first century CE.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/310920749> .

