<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/32694358%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Sacellum of the Augustales";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/432941%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The so-called \"Sacellum of the Augustales\" at Misenum is an architectural complex located near the theater that was first built during the Iulio-Claudian period and dedicated to the Imperial cult. The complex was renovated during the second century, at which time one Cassia Victoria re-dedicated the shrine in honor of her husband, L. Laecanius Primitivus, who was a priest of the Augustales during the reign of Marcus Aurelius.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/32694358> .

