<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/34026796%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Assur Archive 39";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/893945%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "In a room northeast of the courtyard of a private house (in bE8I), excavators found an archive of 29 clay tablets. Two more texts may also belong here. Most of the texts date to the 7th century BC. The archive concerns individuals named Nabu-šar-ahhešu, Sagib-Aššur, and others. It includes both purchase documents and loans.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/34026796> .

