<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/349652620%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Tell Khoshi";
    rdfs:comment "A tell located in Iraq's Sinjar region that was first noted by Seton Lloyd in the mid-1930s. Lloyd conducted limited excavations. Additional fieldwork, including both survey and excavation, took place in the late twentieth and early twenty-first centuries. The site's life began in the middle of the third millennium BCE and continued into the second.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/349652620> .

