<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/352230499%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Guild Temple and Mithraeum of Fructosus";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/422995%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/461688683%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "An architectural complex excavated in 1938 at the intersection of Via del Pomerio and Via del Tempio Rotondo in Ostia. The guild temple dates to the reign of Alexander Severus (222 - 235 CE). Based on epigraphic evidence, this shrine may belong to the guild of the stuppatores. A mithraic shrine with a patron named Fructosus is to be found in the substructure of the podium.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/352230499> .

