    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423025%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Pagus Ianiculens is a name for a district of the Transtiberim during the Republican period. The name is attested in two inscriptions of ca. 100 B.C., one of which was found in an opus signinum pavement near the church of Santa Maria dell'Orto.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/360312699> .

