        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/432833118%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "A quadrifrons triumphal arch at Rome that is located at a crossroads in the area of the Velabrum and the Forum Boarium. It dates to the early fourth century AD; its construction employed spolia, and it likely honored either Constantine I or Constantius II.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/367835399> .

