<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/375818871%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Ager Cosanus survey area";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/117215971%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/403248%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/403280%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413044%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413107%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413192%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413316%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/416769%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/544641873%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/786052704%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/831144251%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The term \"Ager Cosanus\" refers to the territorium (territory) of the Latin right colony of Cosa, reportedly established by Rome in south Etruria in 273 B.C. following conflict with the Etruscan city of Vulci. The colonial center of Cosa has been the subject of ongoing archaeological inquiry since the late 1940s. Beginning in the 1970s, the hinterland of the city was subjected to intensive archaeological field survey. The Wesleyan University survey of the rural hinterland of Cosa identified approximately 132 archaeological sites.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/375818871> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/375821777%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Khorsabad Gate 4";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/175106248%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/21271258%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/4517388%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/874458%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/918508895%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "This undecorated gate is the southernmost city gate of the southeast wall of Dūr-Šarrukīn (\"Fort Sargon\"), the capital of the Assyrian Empire constructed by Sargon II (r. 721–705 BC).";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/375821777> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/375821777/gate-4> dcterms:contributor <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jnovotny>;
    dcterms:description "The modern name assigned to the southernmost gate of Dūr-Šarrukīn's southeast wall. The ancient name of Gate 4 is not known, but it has been suggested that it was the Adad Gate, the Bēlet-ilī Gate, the Ea Gate, and the Šamaš Gate.";
    dcterms:modified "2020-12-27T13:01:54-04:00";
    dcterms:subject "ANE",
