<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/38259712%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Torres de Auençala";
    rdfs:comment "Torres de Auençala was a rural castle located in the west of Jaén. This type of settlement consisted of a fortified perimeter and small tower. This site belonged to the kingdom of Alfonso X (thirteenth century). Today the site is known as Torre Venzalá and is located in Torredonjimeno.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/38259712> .

