<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/386176625%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Kothon";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462373%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The so-called \"Kothon\" is a large, rectangular, artificial pool dating to the Punic period of Sicily and located on the island of Motya. Originally interpreted as an artificial port basin, recent research reinterpets it as a freshwater basin with functions sacred to the god Ba'al and constituting the central component of a large sanctuary.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/386176625> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/386176625/kothon> dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:description "an artificial basin of the Punic phase; verified in Google Earth 2013";
    dcterms:modified "2022-04-28T08:30:22-04:00";
    dcterms:title "Imagery location of Kothon";
    owl:sameAs <http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/386176625/kothon> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/38626420%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Lupanar";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/433032%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/599902893%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The Lupanar (or Lupanare Grande) (VII, 12, 18–20) is located east of the forum at the intersection of Vico del Lupanare and Vico del Balcone Pensile. It is the largest of Pompeii's brothels.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/38626420> .

