<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/387335%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Raudii Campi";
    rdfs:comment "Raudii Campi (or Campus Raudius) is the name of a plain located in Cisalpine Gaul where, in 101 BC, Caius Marius and Catulus defeated the Cimbri. The precise location, perhaps near Verona, is not certain.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/387335> .

