<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/395708592%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Via Minucia / Traiana";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/442511%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/442751%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/442752%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/446273%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The Via Minucia was a Roman road in southern Italy. It was likely built under the Roman consul Marcus Minucius Rufus ca. 110 BCE. It proved to be a poor route for heavy traffic. It likely was used until the early second century CE when the Via Traiana superseded it.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/395708592> .

