    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/265845%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/265950%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "A large and minimally excavated site that lies under the modern Aquisgrana industrial park in the eastern part of the city of La Carolina in Spain's Jaén province. Evidence indicates a temporal span for the site from at least the first century BCE to the late first century CE. The site may have served as a central foundry for metallic ore extracted from mines in and around La Carolina and Cerro del Plomo.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/395991555> .

