    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Schreurs 2024 ";
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/thomase>;
    dcterms:description "An archaeological site in the modern Parc National de l'Isalo in southern Madagascar. The site comprises rock-cut terraces, niches, walls, and other features in a style unique in the region. Radiocarbon dating of charcoal and stylistic dating of imported ceramics place activity at the site to a period spanning the 10th - 12th centuries CE. The excavators tentatively interpret the site as part of a former necropolis made by settlers with Zoroastrian origins.";
    dcterms:modified "2024-10-08T09:07:21-04:00";
