<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/378114380> a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/vocab#Place>;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "ATAE Guzana 2 ",
        "Pedersén 1998 175";
    dcterms:contributor <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/ptushingham>;
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/tseidler>;
    dcterms:description "Inside a clay pot, found in a private house east of the citadel gate of Guzana, excavators discovered the private archive of a man with an Aramaic name, Il-manani, dating to the last years of the Assyrian Empire. The archive consists of five Aramaic dockets concerning loans of barley, previously attached to perishable material, and five clay tablets written in Assyrian cuneiform, specifically three loan documents, one purchase document concerning a slave, and one legal settlement.";
    dcterms:modified "2023-05-11T12:52:58-04:00";
    dcterms:subject "ANE",
        "Assyrian";
    dcterms:title "Guzana Archive 2";
    cito:citesForInformation <http://oracc.museum.upenn.edu/atae/guzana_002>,
        <http://uu.diva-portal.org/smash/get/diva2:88568/FULLTEXT01.pdf>;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/874739>;
    owl:sameAs <http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/378114380>;
    skos:altLabel "Guzana Archive 2"@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places>;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom [ rdfs:label "Pleiades" ];
    pleiades:hasFeatureType <https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/archive-repository>;
    pleiades:hasLocation <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/plan-location-of-guzana-archive-2>;
    pleiades:hasName <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/guzana-archive-2> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/378114381> a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/vocab#Place>;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "ATAE Til-Barsip 1 ",
        "Pedersén 1998 175–176";
    dcterms:contributor <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/thomase>;
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/ptushingham>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/tseidler>;
    dcterms:description "In House C1 in the Lower City of Til-Barsip, 22 Assyrian clay tablets, as well as 2 Aramaic texts, were discovered in and around the doorway between Room XI and XII in a secondary position. The earliest text dates to 683 BC, during the reign of Sennacherib (704-681 BC), but most of the documents date later, to the reign of Ashurbanipal (668-ca. 631 BC). The archive belonged to a man called Hanni, with some of the texts also concerning a man named Ištar-duri, and consists of purchase and loan documents as well as some others, such as a juridicial agreement.";
    dcterms:modified "2023-05-11T12:53:27-04:00";
    dcterms:subject "ANE",
        "Assyrian";
    dcterms:title "Til-Barsip Archive 1";
    cito:citesForInformation <http://oracc.museum.upenn.edu/atae/til_barsip_001>,
        <http://uu.diva-portal.org/smash/get/diva2:88568/FULLTEXT01.pdf>;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/658410>;
    owl:sameAs <http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/378114381>;
    skos:altLabel "Til-Barsip Archive 1"@en;
