    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/39362%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Socotra is an island in the Arabian Sea. It is the eponymous island of the Socotra archipelago and comprises approximately 95% of the landmass in said archipelago. Human activity on the island begins in the Lower Paleolithic. In Graeco-Roman times, the island appears as \"Dioskouridou\" in the Periplus of the Erythraean Sea.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/39338> .

