    dcterms:creator <http://viaf.org/viaf/71459378>,
        <http://viaf.org/viaf/76387372>;
    dcterms:description "The Via Minucia was a Roman road in southern Italy. It was likely built under the Roman consul Marcus Minucius Rufus ca. 110 BCE. It proved to be a poor route for heavy traffic. It likely was used until the early second century CE when the Via Traiana superseded it.";
