    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "AD79 Terrace of M. Nonius Balbus",
        "GeoNames 9794559: Ara di Marco Nonio Balbo",
        "Pompeii Sites La terrazza di M.Nonio Balbo (Terrazza Meridionale, 2)",
        "TrecEnc Zanker, P. \"BALBO, Nonio.\" In Enciclopedia dell' Arte Antica (1994)",
        "Wikidata Q83636890: Terrace and altar of M. Nonius Balbus",
        "Wikipedia (Italian) Marco Nonio Balbo";
    dcterms:contributor <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/thomase>;
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:description "Marcus Nonius Balbus of Nuceria was an important civic patron of Herculaneum. Balbus was a praetor and proconsul of Crete and Cyrene and served as tribune of the plebs in 32 B.C. This architectural complex near the Suburban Baths included the terrace as well as an honorific statue and altar.";
