        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/991334%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Founded by Numidian Berbers, the settlement of Saldae (modern Béjaïa, Algeria) was a minor port during phases of Carthaginian and Roman occupation. The Roman emperor Vespasian established a veteran colony there, at a time when Saldae was part of the province of Mauretania Caesariensis.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/305142> .

